{"findings":[{"id":"9858a1e5-9177-4cef-9c48-af42092a08cf","title":"Some escaped headers are no longer valid JSON strings","description":"For code points above U+FFFF, `oneLine()` now writes `\\u{XXXXX}`, and `\\u{` is not a valid JSON escape. `check` wraps the header in `JSON.stringify` and then passes it through `oneLine`, so a header with a supplementary-plane format character (for example the tag characters U+E0001–U+E007F or U+1D173–U+1D17A) prints a `fail` line whose quoted header fails `JSON.parse`, even though criterion 4 says the header is written as a JSON string. The config error lines (lines 105 and 111) quote the path the same way, so they break in the same way.","category":"Correctness","action_level":"informational","attribution_status":"pending","git_sha":"d0b3721ad0bb46c3c6a21e8e8489f57f5baad95a","location":{"file_path":"src/cli.ts","start_line":126,"end_line":129,"side":"right"},"evidence":{"citations":[{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"src/cli.ts[125-130]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"src/cli.ts[385-389]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"src/cli.ts[105-111]"}]}},{"id":"2978cde6-aeef-4bb6-afb2-bd485f72ae9f","title":"Header doc says unchanged but the text is normalized","description":"The doc comment on `CheckedCommit.header` says it is the \"First line of the commit message, unchanged\", but `checkGitLog` takes it from `ParsedCommit.raw`, which `normalize()` has already stripped of CRs and trailing whitespace. A library caller who reads the exported type will expect git's exact bytes, which also contradicts the revised criterion 4 in the ticket.","category":"Maintainability","action_level":"informational","attribution_status":"pending","git_sha":"d0b3721ad0bb46c3c6a21e8e8489f57f5baad95a","location":{"file_path":"src/check.ts","start_line":17,"end_line":18,"side":"right"},"evidence":{"citations":[{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"src/check.ts[53-58]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"src/commit.ts[124-128]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"tickets/T-009-check-command.md[66-69]"}]}},{"id":"fbd0ecfa-97c6-493a-9ff9-3e267985db29","title":"Check output drops skipped merge commits","description":"The `check` branch in `src/cli.ts` builds stdout from failing commits, malformed records, and the summary without printing `skip <short sha> merge commit` for skipped merges. When the input contains merge commits, maintainers and CI see only the skipped count, and the all-merge test still passes because it checks only the exit code and summary.","category":"Correctness","action_level":"action_required","attribution_status":"pending","git_sha":"d0b3721ad0bb46c3c6a21e8e8489f57f5baad95a","location":{"file_path":"src/cli.ts","start_line":382,"end_line":386,"side":"right"},"evidence":{"citations":[{"source_type":"ticket","source":"https://github.com/UBayouski/tracenotes/issues/27"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"src/cli.ts[382-388]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"tests/cli.test.ts[834-838]"}]}}],"finding_state":{"complete":true,"introduced":["9858a1e5-9177-4cef-9c48-af42092a08cf","2978cde6-aeef-4bb6-afb2-bd485f72ae9f"],"resolved":[],"still_open":["fbd0ecfa-97c6-493a-9ff9-3e267985db29"],"dismissed":[]},"review_agent_comment":"Should `check` exit with code 2 when input yields no commits to check, rather than reporting `checked 0` and succeeding? This may matter when it’s used as a CI lint step, even though the current behavior matches `render`.","meta":{"analysis":{"attempted_mode":"incremental","baseline_checkpoint_id":"9c1d4b50dc884f2e8718ac67f08aa0cc","mode":"full","profile_changed":true,"reason":"delta_scope_unavailable"},"checkpoint":{"base_sha":"d0b3721ad0bb46c3c6a21e8e8489f57f5baad95a","coverage_started_at":"2026-11-19T00:56:50.855197+00:00","created_at":"2026-11-19T00:56:50.855197+00:00","id":"3e0b41af305d42d4bb3a637e610b2729","sequence":35425,"tree_sha":"6767d0332c128cf3b15f4d225a5e66847d52e306","version":1},"context":{"author_notes":{"input_